    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:03.147Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "x402's stated problems solved: eliminating standard-level transaction fees, machine-to-machine payment capability for autonomous AI agents, micropayment infrastructure for granular usage-based monetization, and **permissionless, accountless payment flows**.\n\n**Why it matters:** the account model (signup, API keys, billing relationships) is built for humans and is the main friction for autonomous agents. x402 replaces the account with the payment itself \u2014 possession of funds is the credential.\n\n**Use cases listed:** API monetization, autonomous agent payments, digital content paywalls, microservices monetization, and proxy services reselling API capabilities.\n\nSource: x402 docs introduction (https://docs.x402.org/introduction).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:03.147Z"
    }
  },
